{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk","id":1556192,"title":"Mage/Mummy]Tome of the Pentacle and Marduk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-05T14:22:47-08:00","id":1556192,"title":"Mage/Mummy]Tome of the Pentacle and Marduk","content":"Been reading <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> and came across Marduk. Immaterial but not recognizable as an Ephemeral Entity known, Marduk claimed to be &quot;from the stars&quot; and possessed a strangely unusually high standing of peerage with powerful forces of all kinds.<br /> <br /> Could Marduk have been a Shan'iatu who deserted Irem before the Rite of Return? Maybe some premonition told him trying to get to A'aru was a horrible idea. Maybe he was exiled. Maybe he got cold feet at the last possible moment and hauled ass out of Irem as shit started to go down.<br /> <br /> Could Marduk have been a Shan'iatu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T15:18:51-08:00","id":1556201,"title":"","content":"Seems highly unlikely, given that the First Sothic Turn was centuries before Marduk and part of the Shan'iatu's drive for the Rite of Return was because their wounding by Ammut seems to have cursed them with some level of mortality.<br /> <br /> Some of the stuff about Marduk is drawing from the SAS module &quot;Ruins of Ur,&quot; which came out alongside the Dogs of War supplement on running military stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T16:15:50-08:00","id":1556205,"title":"","content":"Ok. Fill me in, briefly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T19:19:58-08:00","id":1556215,"title":"","content":"Sin being a Nosferatu likely comes from his implicitly being the sire of vampiric antagonist Bashanipal, whose character sheet lists that as his clan. Marduk is a peripheral figure, discussed as a king who thought he was a god but was actually a supernatural being (of unspecified type, with an artifact-guarding evil spirit only knowing he wasn't human). The plot of the SAS is that a team of soldiers has been brought as a meal delivery for Bashanipal under the pretense of escorting an archaeological intelligence mission in Iraq and they need to try to escape and/or thwart the newly-awakened vampire.<br /> <br /> As the timeline outlines, Irem was somewhere between 4000 and 3832 BCE, and Marduk's Babylon was over 1400 years after that, which was far enough apart for the Arisen created with the fall of Irem to wake up; the first chapter of Book of the Deceived provides a fairly extensive account of one of the temakhs indicating they were starting to lose their power before their second audience with the Devourer that gave them the Rite of Return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T22:10:19-08:00","id":1556224,"title":"","content":"Marduk wasn't simply centuries after the First Sothic Turn, he was either almost on the Second or way after even that one, depending on how the book places him in time (I didn't read it, but the Old Babylonian Empire started around 1900 BCE).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T03:13:30-08:00","id":1556231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556224#post1556224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marduk wasn't simply centuries after the First Sothic Turn, he was either almost on the Second or way after even that one, depending on how the book places him in time (I didn't read it, but the Old Babylonian Empire started around 1900 BCE).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good guess. Marduk appears in the <i>TotP</i> timeline at 1950BCE.<br /> <br /> That said, the First Sothic Turn is about 2371BCE, so about 4 centuries out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T09:14:29-08:00","id":1556239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556231#post1556231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good guess. Marduk appears in the <i>TotP</i> timeline at 1950BCE.<br /> <br /> That said, the First Sothic Turn is about 2371BCE, so about 4 centuries out.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this is the second, the first was 3832 BCE, that's why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said Irem was at most at this exact year. Irem fell sometime before the First Sothic Turn, and it marked the first awakening of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> So Marduk appears 4 centuries after the second one, either way too late to be one of the Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> By the way, there are bigger things than the Shan'iatu around, and Marduk may be one of those, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T09:42:55-08:00","id":1556240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556239#post1556239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, this is the second, the first was 3832 BCE, that's why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said Irem was at most at this exact year. Irem fell sometime before the First Sothic Turn, and it marked the first awakening of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> So Marduk appears 4 centuries after the second one, either way too late to be one of the Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> By the way, there are bigger things than the Shan'iatu around, and Marduk may be one of those, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>True. He could be a Supernal Being who figured out how to survive long-term in the Fallen World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:15:34-08:00","id":1556261,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, were the Shan'iatu dying? Or merely growing weaker? <i>Book of the Deceived</i> suggests the latter concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T13:56:09-08:00","id":1556266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556239#post1556239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, this is the second, the first was 3832 BCE, that's why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> said Irem was at most at this exact year.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The First Sothic Turn&quot; refers to the passage of one Sothic Turn after the fall of Irem, when the Arisen first arose. 2371 BCE is directly from the Mummy 1e corebook and Sothis Ascends, the supplement discussing the three Sothic Turns preceding the one corresponding to modern day in 2012 CE; the timeline in the latter book likewise places the Rite of Return and the vanishing of Irem at approximately 3832 BCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T18:18:20-08:00","id":1556324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556266#post1556266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The First Sothic Turn&quot; refers to the passage of one Sothic Turn after the fall of Irem, when the Arisen first arose. 2371 BCE is directly from the Mummy 1e corebook and Sothis Ascends, the supplement discussing the three Sothic Turns preceding the one corresponding to modern day in 2012 CE; the timeline in the latter book likewise places the Rite of Return and the vanishing of Irem at approximately 3832 BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> Either way, Marduk is way after Irem.<br /> <br /> And just as a curiosity: Mummy got the Sothic wrong. In our modern count it's 1460 years, not 1461. It was 1461 in Egyptian years precisely because they didn't had leap years, which made the Sothic Cycle their means to correct for the loss of a day every 4 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T19:50:44-08:00","id":1556329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556324#post1556324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just as a curiosity: Mummy got the Sothic wrong. In our modern count it's 1460 years, not 1461. It was 1461 in Egyptian years precisely because they didn't had leap years, which made the Sothic Cycle their means to correct for the loss of a day every 4 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book also says 1,460 years in both corebooks' lexicon and the Introduction to Sothis Ascends specifies solar years, so this is almost definitely a case of miscommunication between writers for different parts of the book.<br /> <br /> The earliest point on the timeline for &quot;Sothic Turn Zero&quot; consistently has &quot;approximate year estimate&quot; markers on it, and to the best of my knowledge there's negligible obvious historic differences to be found in an off-by-one error that has only repeated itself four times so far, particularly given the establishment of ancient history and prehistory in the Chronicles of Darkness being extremely strange to those with the ability to magically investigate it.<br /> <br /> If we were to treat the estimated start point as accurate then the listed years will only be halfway toward being a decade off another 1450+ years from now, and since the intention was that the Fourth Sothic Turn coincided with the release year of the gameline (and the various eschatological beliefs revolving around 2012) the more practical outcome is that the estimated start point is ~3828 BCE, with the First Turn being in 2368 BCE, the Second Turn being in 908 BCE, and the Third Turn being in 552 CE; the projected Fifth Turn is only described temporally in terms of what century it will be in, and that's a speculative story hook where the characters wake up on Mars or a ruined Earth as part of 2e's introduction of the Timeless Chronicle as a corebook tool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Going back to things being too late to be Shan'iatu, it <i>is</i> perhaps worth noting that Sothis Ascends has a sidebar on what's up with Imhotep and why Kemet's religion diverges so prominently from Irem's between the Rite of Return and the First Sothic Turn, and one of the things the Arisen speculate he might have been is &quot;a Shan'iatu born millennia too late,&quot; so at the very least there's some legs to the idea as a rumor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T11:57:39-08:00","id":1556350,"title":"","content":"I completely agree that the difference is negligible, it's just a curiosity, and thanks for the &quot;corrected&quot; timeline..<br /> <br /> Personally I would prefer Imhotep to be something else than a Shan'iatu, as this seems the Path of Least Creativity to me. But Marduk seems even more off given the distance from Kemet. Not strictly impossible, but I find it both uninspired and unlikely, so unless there's a real need by the plot of a chronicle, I'd pass on having him be a Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> Granted, it's perfectly possible for a good plot to require what would otherwise be an unlikely and uninspired thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:14:50-08:00","id":1556352,"title":"","content":"So...what would Marduk be?<br /> <br /> Let's look at what we know:<br /> \u25cf He's an Ephemeral Entity, though not of any kind known to his era.<br /> \u25cf He has to have a vessel to work or rest in----no Manifestations of note perhaps?<br /> \u25cf He wanted stability throughout Mesopotamia.<br /> \u25cf He held high enough status among the Powers That Be (which included the Exarchs) to ENFORCE this stability.<br /> \u25cf He was given a gilded trap in the form of his idol, which he seemed to sleep longer and longer periods of time inside.<br /> \u25cf When his idol, which carried his sleeping Essence, was stolen by invaders, he went silent forever. Was he slain?<br /> \u25cf It's pretty heavily hinted the Exarchs were involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:00:20-08:00","id":1556361,"title":"","content":"And <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> flat-out states Imhotep was a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:22:26-08:00","id":1556363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He was given a gilded trap in the form of his idol, which he seemed to sleep longer and longer periods of time inside. </div> </div> </div>It's not implausible, but I wouldn't say we know this for certain. Perhaps Marduk would have gradually weakened whatever happened, and the statue merely allowed him to eke out his limited power for longer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So...what would Marduk be? </div> </div> </div>As an aside, I think in the original <i>Ruins of Ur</i>, he's intended to be some kind of vampire. That said, it's a very odd story and probably not that relevant.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:29:03-08:00","id":1556366,"title":"","content":"<i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> outright states Marduk's an Ephemeral Entity of unknown type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T16:27:59-08:00","id":1556373,"title":"","content":"Michael:<br /> The mage who made Marduk's idol was basically a proto-Seer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T03:29:40-08:00","id":1556377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556373#post1556373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael:<br /> The mage who made Marduk's idol was basically a proto-Seer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it doesn't actually say that, but probably. We're told that <i>modern mages</i> consider the Barutu as a group to be precursors to the Seers, but what that means practically isn't made entirely clear beyond the fact that prelates are clearly accorded a lot of respect and importance.<br /> <br /> More to the point, does it matter? It doesn't contradict what I suggested. Like, keeping Marduk around isn't necessarily a benevolent act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:43:19-08:00","id":1556385,"title":"","content":"No, but they plotted his downfall. If he was useful to the Exarchs, then that use had a limited shelflife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:47:43-08:00","id":1556386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556385#post1556385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but they plotted his downfall. If he was useful to the Exarchs, then that use had a limited shelflife.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, how do you know this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:48:14-08:00","id":1556387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556352#post1556352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what would Marduk be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything, really, including something unique.<br /> <br /> CofD is made to let you achieve a given result through infinite means, so you're not completely sure of what anything is. Even among the major splats there are some that aren't necessarily the same thing beyond following some similar rules, Vampires, Deviants and Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Marduk can be any type of high-ranking Ephemeral Entity, because above Rank 6 it becomes virtually impossible to tell them apart with certainty. He may be a splat and have achieved Ephemeral-like status through any number of means, accessible to PCs or not. And he may be like many other unique beings or weird local species there are in the setting.<br /> <br /> What matters isn't what Marduk is so much as what would be interesting to make him be in a given chronicle, and I don't see a particular answer sticking out. Unique being would be the simplest, a god of sorts that can't be related to any other phenomenon, so must be researched and dealt with on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:31:47-08:00","id":1556392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556386#post1556386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, how do you know this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude had a Prelacy. That requires knowing service to an Exarch. Hence why I said he was a proto-Seer. He made the idol as a gift to Marduk. Mardyk became more and sleepy as a result. Then, after foreign invaders stole Marduk's idol, the entity seems to have...[idisappeared[/i]!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:49:01-08:00","id":1556393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556352#post1556352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what would Marduk be?<br /> <br /> Let's look at what we know:<br /> \u25cf He's an Ephemeral Entity, though not of any kind known to his era.<br /> \u25cf He has to have a vessel to work or rest in----no Manifestations of note perhaps?<br /> \u25cf He wanted stability throughout Mesopotamia.<br /> \u25cf He held high enough status among the Powers That Be (which included the Exarchs) to ENFORCE this stability.<br /> \u25cf He was given a gilded trap in the form of his idol, which he seemed to sleep longer and longer periods of time inside.<br /> \u25cf When his idol, which carried his sleeping Essence, was stolen by invaders, he went silent forever. Was he slain?<br /> \u25cf It's pretty heavily hinted the Exarchs were involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's up to the Storyteller, here is one idea of what he could be:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Marduk is the embodiment of the original name of The Gate. The ritual to Ascend as the Exarch of the Abyss was paradoxical, you needed to cut out their name so they could take on the title of The Gate. The candidate had to be a paradox too, someone who aligned more with the Oracle's principles, but was doing an Exarch's job. Hence his unique nature, power and leverage, he was a living name. The Exarchs need the Gate and were initially on board with his divine kingship, but when started to become a thorn on their side, they started to figure out how to undermine and contain him. He is probably a Bound in modern times. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:50:38-08:00","id":1556394,"title":"","content":"A Bound mage? Or a Bound Ochema?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T10:09:09-08:00","id":1556396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556394#post1556394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Bound mage? Or a Bound Ochema?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Neither, a severed part of the original mage, a sentient Seba with astral characteristics (because names are as connected to Mind as they are to Fate). Think about <i>the Month of Darkness</i> song in <i>Dishonored 2</i>. The Outsider as a mortal did not want to be the god of the void, but the cultists had a use for him, so they ritually sacrificed him and cut out his name, now he had to do the job. The name of the Outsider became the mark that grants supernatural powers in both games. In the case of The Gate, the name still had sentience and a will.<br /> <br /> In modern times, I guess he is sealed in some kind of repurposed prison of the Tef-Aabhi, with an Iron Seal on top of it. Kept sealed with the power of <i>heka</i> and Supernal wardens, in addition to whatever Seers unknowingly watch over such a valuable prisoner. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T10:11:04-08:00","id":1556397,"title":"","content":"...<i>not</i> the answer i was expecting, but as I love crossover, it is an answer i find approoriate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T11:40:38-08:00","id":1556432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556392#post1556392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude had a Prelacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mardyk became more and sleepy <i>as a result.</i> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say that. It says he became increasingly reliant on it, that's not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T12:06:24-08:00","id":1556435,"title":"","content":"He was Barutu...who worshipped the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> <i>And</i> Marduk slept more often than before, once inside the idol a proto-Seer made for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28921,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","user":"CreatorFounderMaker","date":". 12-10-2025, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T13:08:31-08:00","id":1556437,"title":"","content":"[Wrong post location]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-10-2025, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T13:21:35-08:00","id":1556483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556435#post1556435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was Barutu...<b>who worshipped the Exarchs.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say that. The description we get of the Barutu is that it was a great cult where proto-Seers were able to gain a lot of influence. Otherwise, there's no real reason to think it didn't operate like other Great Cults with multiple Schools beyond those directly serving the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> That said, there's also a lot more ambiguity over what 'worshipping' an Exarch would even mean in this era. Like, the Pelasgians from <i>To The Strongest</i> 'worship' the Exarchs in a certain sense, but they also seem to hold them in a degree of contempt. There's clearly a gap between thinking the 'Gods' should be respected and perhaps listened to to a limited extent, and being a full-on prelate in service to the throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>And</i> Marduk slept more often than before... </div> </div> </div>It seems to suggest he only slept after given the statue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...once inside the idol a <b>proto-Seer</b> made for him. </div> </div> </div>We don't know that. Indeed, the 'proto-Seer' tag is given to the Fourfold and their associates who preceded the Barutu. The Barutu itself is referred to as a 'precursor' to the Seers, but that's qualified as an opinion of modern mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T07:17:09-08:00","id":1556556,"title":"","content":"I find myself thinking that, given Marduk's position in the setting, the main determining factor of what he would have been shouldn't be in trying to derive something from all the minor details provided but what makes a compelling outcome to any modern day characters investigating the Mystery of him.<br /> <br /> That <i>does</i> allow for the possibility of uncovering evidence of a Bronze Age society governed by a spirit that had managed to start running along some unconventional lines or a Supernal entity who was fixed without being Bound.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm the type who's generally inclined to lean Mysteries in the direction of &quot;more between Heaven and Earth than dreamt of in your philosophies&quot; more often than not. My own priority for the outcome of investigating the Mystery of how an ancient society was governed by a supernatural entity would be to fold that into a larger Mystery of how and why so many types of supernatural entity, including ones difficult to categorise, could govern openly in a different era of the world, and what changed. The outcome of the question of &quot;what was Marduk&quot; becomes &quot;why is Marduk not anymore&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Even if on a practical level the tone and scope of a lot of Chronicles games is likely to render the initial conclusions about Marduk as an unsettling hanging question that never gets resolved.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T09:50:29-08:00","id":1556559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556556#post1556556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own priority for the outcome of investigating the Mystery of how an ancient society was governed by a supernatural entity would be to fold that into a larger Mystery of how and why so many types of supernatural entity, including ones difficult to categorise, could govern openly in a different era of the world, and what changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the less consistent parts of the timeline is that we aren't really given clear examples of the open supernatural rule that it mentions as coming to an end. Like, most of the examples are not that dissimilar to how supernatural beings work for the rest of history.<br /> <br /> For example, Marduk doesn't seem to be running Babylon openly, he works through the line of kings; and it's not like the mortals stop worshipping him after he disappears.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 12-13-2025, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T12:10:53-08:00","id":1556565,"title":"","content":"True. Some Mysteries might be unsolvable by anything less than a top-tier archmage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T00:44:53-08:00","id":1556593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556559#post1556559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the less consistent parts of the timeline is that we aren't really given clear examples of the open supernatural rule that it mentions as coming to an end. Like, most of the examples are not that dissimilar to how supernatural beings work for the rest of history.<br /> <br /> For example, Marduk doesn't seem to be running Babylon openly, he works through the line of kings; and it's not like the mortals stop worshipping him after he disappears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem here is that the game has to partially reconcile fictional history with RL history. Since the line of kings is a well established fact, it must have existed within the setting.<br /> <br /> That said, the use of intermediaries doesn't necessarily means hidden. There are lots of public figures with huge amounts of power, money and influence, formal or not, that work by proxy for one reason or another. In some countries most of the actual power resides with a party chairman that isn't formally head of state. In others you have monarchies with varying degrees of legal powers plus <b><i>a lot</i></b> of influence even if they're formally just a ceremonial role. Others yet have religious figures that command the country in all but name. Not to say of how many rich celebrities have a completely disproportional <i>and publicly known </i>sway over politics despite not being an official part of the government.<br /> <br /> Marduk was a known figure, that's beyond any doubt. How many humans in the setting can name the supernatural masters of their city? There could be many ways in which he was an open ruler at the same time he had kings under him, either as proxies, messengers, or actual rulers that had nonetheless to obey him in public displays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T04:30:48-08:00","id":1556602,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the problem here is that the game has to partially reconcile fictional history with RL history. Since the line of kings is a well established fact, it must have existed within the setting. </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's more just an issue for Marduk specifically. My point is that the timeline says that the Bronze Age Collapse marked the end of beings such as Marduk openly ruling... But what we're told about is mostly supernatural beings already working through intermediaries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, the use of intermediaries doesn't necessarily means hidden. There are lots of public figures with huge amounts of power, money and influence, formal or not, that work by proxy for one reason or another. In some countries most of the actual power resides with a party chairman that isn't formally head of state. In others you have monarchies with varying degrees of legal powers plus <b><i>a lot</i></b> of influence even if they're formally just a ceremonial role. Others yet have religious figures that command the country in all but name. Not to say of how many rich celebrities have a completely disproportional <i>and publicly known </i>sway over politics despite not being an official part of the government. </div> </div> </div>This is kinda my point. Like, it's not obvious that anything has changed after the Bronze Age Collapse. Alexander and his successors a millennia later are surrounded by mages trying to influence them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marduk was a known figure, that's beyond any doubt. How many humans in the setting can name the supernatural masters of their city? </div> </div> </div>Sure, but he seems kinda exceptional in being more or less what he appears to be. To compare, we also have Sin the Nosferatu, who lives in a city where the people worship a moon deity called Sin... Is that open rule? Like, the people know his name, but they've radically misunderstood what he is.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>is</i> that his name? Like, I gather the deity Marduk predates the arrival of 'Marduk' in Babylon by a few centuries. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There could be many ways in which he was an open ruler at the same time he had kings under him, either as proxies, messengers, or actual rulers that had nonetheless to obey him in public displays. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but those public displays are going to continue for centuries after he disappears. That implies that as far as the people of Babylon are concerned, it doesn't really matter whether he's present or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T06:37:38-08:00","id":1556603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556602#post1556602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, that's more just an issue for Marduk specifically. My point is that the timeline says that the Bronze Age Collapse marked the end of beings such as Marduk openly ruling... But what we're told about is mostly supernatural beings already working through intermediaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to look back at the chapter, but I recall a sense that the distinction was the the supernatural beings and empowered people were open about what they were and actively positioning themselves in a place in the social hierarchy adjacent to mortal authorities. The mages in To The Strongest seem to have become more subtle and distant by habit and necessity.<br /> <br /> True, even within that context, there seem to have been holdouts of the old model, even if they were on the way out. We're told that the Iranian Great Cult are assuming a power vacuum left by the preceding form of being embedded in the Zoroastrian priesthood, and the Egyptian cult had been holding the position of high priests for longer than might be expected. But then again, the Acaemenid Empire was not founded until <i>well</i> after the Bronze Age collapse, and even if Zoroastrianism dates back much further, it being a significant social influence seems to coincide with that empire's founding, so that's not really a Great Cult in the ancient model surviving so much as a new one rising from scratch in a context that might have risen to a similar position had it not been violently interrupted (with the Bronze Age Iranian plateau otherwise having been part of the cultural sphere of Mesopotamia). And I recall the Egyptians having a tone of being far from their heyday in a manner that might imply still being in a state of recovery from disaster.<br /> <br /> The way you're referring back to Marduk makes me think of the arrangement in the Nameless Empire, where even the Shan'iatu did not technically rule directly and had a mortal human pharaoh to function as a ceremonial stand in for Azar whom they are technically deferential to. And yet, I think most people would read the Shan'iatu as having been the actual authorities of the empire, and would not regard that relationship is indistinguishable from the shadowy conspiracy of modern supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556602#post1556602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but those public displays are going to continue for centuries after he disappears. That implies that as far as the people of Babylon are concerned, it doesn't really matter whether he's present or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the people of North Korea are concerned, Kim il-Sung is still president, but the public performance of such is not directly equivalent to him actually being around to do stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-14-2025, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T06:41:08-08:00","id":1556604,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty safe to say from practical, tactical, and gameline-historical perspectives that the threshold for &quot;open supernatural rule&quot; is just &quot;this place is run by a supernatural being of some kind and this is a matter of unhidden public knowledge&quot; \u2014 Marduk possessing the kings of Babylon in the earlier part of his rule doesn't remove the strategic/social pressures that led the Kindred of Transylvania to spread word of the banes of the Strix that bedeviled them, and Irem is <i>right there</i> as an example where even their military supremacy wasn't a matter of having zombie armies or wings of fire so much as knowing how to use troop formations and proper metallurgy to train and arm their mortal soldiers (with relics being a subtler and more portable/less vital force multiplier to be deployed where necessary).<br /> <br /> To borrow from Vampire's usual line of thought that derives into the Masquerade centuries later, it's one thing for your subjects to know you have magic powers and a whole different thing for them to know you're a specific subtype of monster with particular weaknesses and limitations that can be exploited. The pretenses of omniscience and immortality alone go a long way when attached to state power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T08:04:49-08:00","id":1556609,"title":"","content":"So, while we know what <i>mundanely</i> caused the collapse, what supernatural agency might be responsible?<br /> <br /> My theory is two-fold: a cooperative act of the Exarchs and the God-Machine<br /> <br /> The Exarchs, while greater than all other beings, <i>don't</i> rule the universe <i>unchallenged</i>. This may've been a significant step towards establishing greater authority for themselves.<br /> <br /> As for the God-Machibe, it seems to care about supernaturals ruling openly. It's content to let them be, as long as they remain 'hidden' from the heaving masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T14:15:02-08:00","id":1556624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556609#post1556609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while we know what <i>mundanely</i> caused the collapse</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, part of why it's possible to write a setting history like this is because we really don't. We can't. Even apart from the fact that it is an event that, by its nature, erases a lot of what provides us with information about the past (literate society and monumental architecture), there's just fundamentally a huge gulf of information that comes from the separation of three thousand years.<br /> <br /> We can make informed guesses, and reasonably assume that the evidence points to something at least resembling a collapse, but certainty as to how or why is impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T15:14:26-08:00","id":1556625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556624#post1556624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, part of why it's possible to write a setting history like this is because we really don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the timeline gives us an answer for the purposes of the <i>CofD</i>. There are a couple of events in the timeline that I gather are merely likely.<br /> <br /> That said, the Bronze Age Collapse described seems significantly worse than the one in history (admittedly, it's quite vague). Like, being the Mesopotamian Great Cult, the Barutu should have been largely unaffected by the Collapse. The Middle Assyrian Empire just keeps on going. (It does mention that the prelates stop getting messages, which is certainly material for explaining why the Barutu collapsed, but it seems pretty clear that it's meant to be the Collapse that does them in.)<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, both Babylon and Ur aren't destroyed by the collapse. So Marduk is still openly ruling a city despite not actually being around anymore, and presumably Sin just keeps ruling Ur down to it's abandonment in the 5th century BCE. (Or not depending on what we make of <i>Ruins of Ur</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T09:09:51-08:00","id":1556653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556625#post1556625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the Bronze Age Collapse described seems significantly worse than the one in history (admittedly, it's quite vague). Like, being the Mesopotamian Great Cult, the Barutu should have been largely unaffected by the Collapse. The Middle Assyrian Empire just keeps on going. (It does mention that the prelates stop getting messages, which is certainly material for explaining why the Barutu collapsed, but it seems pretty clear that it's meant to be the Collapse that does them in.)</div> </div> </div> </div>One could possibly read into the point that there are not only centuries between the apparent end of Marduk and the period given for the collapse, but that the Baratu seem like a Great Cult that was heavily intertwined with Marduk's rise and fall in the first place. It's possible that with that purpose accomplished, the cult was kind of defunct, and over the centuries drifted away.<br /> <br /> The book <i>does</i> still say that there were powerful states that survived, so the Assyrian Empire can adhere to that. Babylon arguably no longer qualified as openly ruled by the supernatural enough to be completely targeted for ruin, so I think the points could be reconciled with an idea of &quot;between a bit of enhanced reality and historical blind spots, Sumer was just affected enough to disrupt whatever remained of its mage society, in keeping with the overall desired tone for heading into the Scholastic Age&quot;.<br /> <br /> It probably is a bit of an awkward fit, but if Babylon is important enough to have prominence in the Sundered Age (and they want to build something about the history of the Hittites stealing the Marduk idol), but doesn't really fit into what they want to be the backstory to the context of To The Strongest, they have to work with what they've got, and I think informed readers should try to meet them in the middle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Marduk is still openly ruling a city despite not actually being around anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what you mean by this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T09:23:35-08:00","id":1556654,"title":"","content":"I don't either. Absent leaders silenced forever give no further orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T18:55:50-08:00","id":1556687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556192-mage-mummy-tome-of-the-pentacle-and-marduk?p=1556654#post1556654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't either. Absent leaders silenced forever give no further orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not unlike Kim il-Sung being the current president of North Korea despite being dead.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way, it's being too attached to formal titles and ignoring actual power structures.<br /> <br /> Before the colapse Marduk ruled directly and publicly. Regardless if there were other positions and titles, including a king (that wasn't actually called a king and wasn't necessarily a king in the sense we understand it), if Marduk was his real name or if people knew what exactly he was, what makes him an open supernatural ruler is that he had <i>de facto</i> power, and both that and him being a powerful supernatural entity were publicly known facts.<br /> <br /> So much so that, centuries after his rule, his name and legend were still widely known, while current supernatural rulers will never be a part of known history in any way, no one will ever know they even were there.<br /> <br /> The fact that after his fall from open rule Marduk was still worshiped as a god is a statement to the fact that he was openly the ruler and supernatural. But it doesn't change the fact that it's still a completely different situation, where it became a matter of ritual, tradition and belief, of ceremony, and not anymore about people really expecting this super-powered man to show up and shout orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}